<title>UK: JKX says payments start for Ukraine gas JV.</title>
<headline>JKX says payments start for Ukraine gas JV.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>British exploration group JKX Oil &amp; Gas Plc said on Friday payments had commenced for natural gas supplied by its Ukrainian joint venture Poltava Petroleum Co (PPC) under an agreement with state-owned UKRAGAS.</p>
<p>Two payments totalling $540,000 have been received, JKX said in a statement.</p>
<p>The agreement covers the sale of 227 million cubic metres of storage gas and PPC's available gas production for the remainder of 1997. PPC had supplied 312 million cubic metres, including the storage gas, by the end of June.</p>
<p>JKX owns 49 percent of PPC.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
